{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals","id":1463328,"title":"Magnanimous Totem, Moon's Grace and Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-10T10:56:55-07:00","id":1463328,"title":"Magnanimous Totem, Moon's Grace and Supernaturals","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have a couple of questions regarding pack merits: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does the <b>Magnanimous Totem</b> merit allow other supernaturals to buy Totem dots? If so, at what rating?</li> <li>Are the benefits granted by <b>Moon's Grace</b> usable by other supernaturals?</li> </ol><br /> I am thinking mostly human templates should benefit in both cases, like all minor templates (Ghouls, Stigmatics, Fae-Touched, etc), and perhaps Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T18:11:08-07:00","id":1463357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals#post1463328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the <b>Magnanimous Totem</b> merit allow other supernaturals to buy Totem dots? If so, at what rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Wolf-Blooded or humans only. Non supernatural (including mages.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are the benefits granted by <b>Moon's Grace</b> usable by other supernaturals? </div> </div> </div>As before. Wolf-Blooded and humans only, not supernaturals. If extending it to minor templates works for you game, then do it. But RAW, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:08:31-07:00","id":1464343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1463357#post1463357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Wolf-Blooded or humans only. Non supernatural (including mages.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As before. Wolf-Blooded and humans only, not supernaturals. If extending it to minor templates works for you game, then do it. But RAW, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does RAW mean? In any case, you made a mistake. I have the book and double checked. <br /> <br /> Those merits never specify what it doesn't apply to, only what it does apply to. In that context, it offers no commentary on overlapping categories. Whether you are right or left-handed, can read English or Spanish, or are pre-teen or geriatric, it doesn't elaborate. <br /> <br /> Similarly, it says nothing about the supernatural. Remember that the Wolf-blooded are supernatural and Mages are still human. I cannot say for certain that Mages are included, but neither can you say they aren't, as though there was a way either of us could know that. There just wasn't any clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:23:23-07:00","id":1464347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1464343#post1464343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does RAW mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written. You may also sometimes see RAI - rules as intended - which is what I\u2019m also giving here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, you made a mistake. I have the book and double checked. </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t, but whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those merits never specify what it doesn't apply to, only what it does apply to. </div> </div> </div>It DOES apply to these things means it DOESN\u2019T apply to things that are not those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether you are right or left-handed, can read English or Spanish, or are pre-teen or geriatric, it doesn't elaborate. </div> </div> </div>Because if you\u2019re Wolf-Blooded or human, the Merit couldn\u2019t care less about your handedness, linguistic ability, or age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cannot say for certain that Mages are included, but neither can you say they aren't, as though there was a way either of us could know that. </div> </div> </div>Look, you do what you want, I don\u2019t care how you play your games or what happens at your table. If it\u2019s fun for your group, that\u2019s the only thing I care about. However, I can 100% say with absolute certainty and no confusion or hesitation that Mages aren\u2019t included, nor are anything except Wolf-Blooded and (non supernatural) humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-18-2021, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:13:22-07:00","id":1464358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1464347#post1464347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rules as written. You may also sometimes see RAI - rules as intended - which is what I\u2019m also giving here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t, but whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It DOES apply to these things means it DOESN\u2019T apply to things that are not those things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because if you\u2019re Wolf-Blooded or human, the Merit couldn\u2019t care less about your handedness, linguistic ability, or age.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look, you do what you want, I don\u2019t care how you play your games or what happens at your table. If it\u2019s fun for your group, that\u2019s the only thing I care about. However, I can 100% say with absolute certainty and no confusion or hesitation that Mages aren\u2019t included, nor are anything except Wolf-Blooded and (non supernatural) humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed my point. Mages are human, the merit says humans are included. That is what I meant by &quot;overlapping categories&quot;. Your third response ignores what I actually said. Mages &quot;are those things&quot;. You also admit that other characteristics don't matter, like language or handedness, so why does being supernatural matter where those don't? You didn't make an argument, you just reasserted without citation that the merit had a qualifier I can't find in my copy of the book.<br /> <br /> Where is the qualifier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:32:16-07:00","id":1464365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1464358#post1464358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t, but you missed my point. I don\u2019t care what you do at your table as long as you\u2019re having fun. But for the benefit of Ibeaumanior who asked the original question, I can tell them precisely what was intended by the merits. No mages, no supernatural, baseline humans only, with Wolf-Blooded as the exception.<br /> <br /> But, repeating this on a separate line because it\u2019s important, what individual groups choose to do is absolutely fine if it works for them because it\u2019s a game and it\u2019s about having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:51:16-07:00","id":1464381,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify,<br /> Mages are NOT humans.<br /> Their bodies are still human.<br /> Their souls are supernatural, not different from that of other major splats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:25:59-07:00","id":1464402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1463357#post1463357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Wolf-Blooded or humans only. Non supernatural (including mages.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this was something I've had a question about for a while now. Obviously Werewolf is not beholden to address crossover outside of the times it explcitly comes up, and keeping the merit to humans/wolf-blooded is one of those small touches to keep the Forsaken....forsaken, but was there any additional reasoning behind keeping it to that set?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:36:04-07:00","id":1464404,"title":"","content":"I think the idea was supernatural splats override the human. Like with chronicles 1st (I know I know) you started with the human template, and anything else you had was over ridden by the supernatural template to such a degree that you weren\u2019t spiritually compatible with the other. Vampires being dead and spiritless, and mages being a different brand of awake vs the wolves and wolf blooded. <br /> <br /> At least that\u2019s how I understood it. I\u2019d think a mage might look alien, or even terrifying to a totem depending on its level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T13:13:18-07:00","id":1464411,"title":"","content":"Souls are so ill defined you could just say they have spurs that cause them to not fit under Magnanimous or just 'Awakening makes it unavailable' like so many other things. And Luna can just prefer not to grant her grace to mages after seeing how the they've posted about white room versions of her.<br /> <br /> But if things like 'Your third nipple disappears and you stop being Fuck Ugly' upon Awakening get a pass on needing explanation I'm not sure why these Merits need the hard facts beyond a desire to argue over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-18-2021, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T15:30:01-07:00","id":1464537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1464402#post1464402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, this was something I've had a question about for a while now. Obviously Werewolf is not beholden to address crossover outside of the times it explcitly comes up, and keeping the merit to humans/wolf-blooded is one of those small touches to keep the Forsaken....forsaken, but was there any additional reasoning behind keeping it to that set?</div> </div> </div> </div>In universe, it\u2019s about the nature of the pack, the nature of the connection between spirit and Uratha, and the way Luna interacts with her children.<br /> <br /> It comes from the nature of the Uratha soul*, and the \u2018spaces\u2019 it has for connection to the spiritual side of their nature. Uratha have a space where Auspice connects them to Luna, a space for connection to the Firstborn and tribe, one for their totem etc. For Pure, when they remove their Auspices, we see that they have additional space for their Firstborn to fill in the form of Hunter\u2019s Aspects.<br /> <br /> These spaces don\u2019t all just come spontaneously from the First Change. There\u2019s first something to work from, something with the right kind of shape that can be further reformed to deliver the desired outcome. Just like humanity gives the Uratha their basic four limbs, one head, two-eyes, two-ears, hair-covered template, the human soul already has \u2018built in\u2019 the potential for transformation into the necessary Uratha-required spiritual shape. When the First Change happens, Luna (through whatever force she has in place) reshapes the body and soul from human to Uratha.<br /> <br /> That sets the foundation, and sets the scene for why the merits only apply to WB and humans. WB are already part-way towards reshaping as Uratha. Their bodies and souls are partially transformed in a variety of ways depending on their Tells. It\u2019s relatively small effort for Luna/totem spirits to make the rest of the changes necessary for the WB to gain full access to the connections allowing some Uratha-like advantages. It\u2019s more effort to make those same changes in humans, but still possible, if the spiritual sponsor wants to make the effort. (The relative amount of effort is represented by how may Merit points the characters have to spend to access these advantages.)<br /> <br /> Other templates - major or minor - can\u2019t access these advantages because they\u2019ve chosen (or had chosen for them) to go down other paths. Their souls have been twisted away from the shapes spirit creatures can more easily work with, or they\u2019ve filled them with something else. Vampires and mages may look human, but they\u2019re not when it comes to having the foundations of Uratha-potential. Similarly, Ghouls, Sleepwalkers, or whatever other minor templates have gummed up their accessibility as well, spirits can\u2019t latch onto their souls in the right way to give access to the Uratha-like advantages, which results from a game perspective of those characters not being able to purchase the Merits.<br /> <br /> *I\u2019m using the term \u2018soul\u2019 generically here. I know it has a lot of baggage in CoD but it\u2019s an easy word to use for this explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-19-2021, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T16:21:01-07:00","id":1464540,"title":"","content":"That tracks, and even neatly slots in about the potential energy turned kinetic with Divergence, as well as humanity's capacity for slasherdom and Beastdom, and a couple of the other loose ends-at least, in the rough &quot;shape&quot; my head correlates them together with.<br /> <br /> When it came to the table practice, I never particularly stressed about supernaturals getting to contribute to Totem, while I went the exact opposite on Moon's Grace and doubled down, but I figured there was a good reason for the RAW, and this definitely satisfies the Watsonian take, particularly with the assumed Doylist reasons I already had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T16:38:23-07:00","id":1464541,"title":"","content":"I also have no probelm with people allowing access to the Merit to supernaturals. Whatever works at the table, and if people want mixed groups with different supernaturals in the pack it makes life easier. <br /> <br /> But RAW, we were keeping it slightly more locked down. Luna loves her children and the humans who copy them. She doesn't have the same attachment to other supernaturals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:55:00-07:00","id":1465781,"title":"","content":"Curious - RAW, are wolf-blooded that become something else but keep their Tell wolf-blooded 'enough' to still retain this Merit if they had it previously? <br /> Or is the Tell more like a metaphysical 'scar' at that point, vs a still-active connection to the Pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T10:26:13-07:00","id":1465787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1463328-magnanimous-totem-moon-s-grace-and-supernaturals?p=1465781#post1465781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious - RAW, are wolf-blooded that become something else but keep their Tell wolf-blooded 'enough' to still retain this Merit if they had it previously?<br /> Or is the Tell more like a metaphysical 'scar' at that point, vs a still-active connection to the Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stictly speaking, a lot of the &quot;become something else&quot; category of things is enough that it effectively wipes out all metaphysical connection of the Wolf-Blooded template-that inheritance isn't going to stand up to the transformation of a Durance or recontextualization of an Awakening.<br /> <br /> But it's a post-Contagion world, and in particular a post-ContagionPG world-the general rule of &quot;If you can personally grok it and have have fun with it, then go for it&quot; has been more firmly placed as the major component of the whole of the law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-29-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}